text:
Final Private Lesson (for now!)

Heya y'all! Just had my final private lesson for a couple weeks... and yeah, it went great! It feels like my underwater endurance is getting better, which is reassuring, and front crawl with a board isn't too bad!

&#x200B;

...that being said, without a board, the rotation part of front crawl is... rough. It's something I will definitely need to practice a bit to get used to. We used flippers today to let me get used to the rotation... and well, it wasn't flawless, but I'm working on it! And flippers are certainly very fun to use :D

&#x200B;

I got a stretch of 4 lessons in a couple weeks here, and before then, I plan to go to the local pool again to practice. Until then, any advice on how to get better at front crawl rotation would be welcome! :)
